From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:52:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: make the thread info key once on iOS, not at every
 process's load

On iOS every guest process of the session runs in one host process and
shares win32u's unix library, whose __wine_unix_lib_init runs at each
guest process's win32u load. Each run made a new user_thread_info key
and stored it over the old one, so when a second process loaded win32u
(a launcher's game, a game's crash reporter or dxdiag child, a
prerequisite installer) every thread of the processes already running
found no user_thread_info under the new key and got a fresh, empty one:
its message queue handle, desktop and message windows, hook state,
message being received and OpenGL thread data were gone, and the old
ones leaked. The key is now made once (pthread_once).
KeAddSystemServiceTable and ntdll_add_syscall_debug_info set the same
table and names again, and wow64_zero_bits the same mask (0027), so
they stay as they are.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-12-prefix-loader-leftovers.md
Offered-upstream: no; iOS-only (one process for every guest process)
---
 dlls/win32u/syscall.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/syscall.c b/dlls/win32u/syscall.c
index 94206e2..fce2684 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/syscall.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/syscall.c
@@ -174,6 +174,20 @@ static const char *usercall_names[NtUserCallCount] =
 
 static pthread_key_t user_thread_info_key;
 
+#ifdef WINE_IOS
+/* On iOS every guest process of the session shares this library, and this
+ * init runs at each process's win32u load: the key is made once, or a later
+ * process's load would replace it and the threads of the processes already
+ * running would lose their user_thread_info (queue, windows, hooks, OpenGL
+ * data). KeAddSystemServiceTable and the debug names set the same values again. */
+static pthread_once_t user_thread_info_once = PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT;
+
+static void create_user_thread_info_key(void)
+{
+    pthread_key_create( &user_thread_info_key, NULL );
+}
+#endif
+
 NTSTATUS __wine_unix_lib_init(void)
 {
 #ifdef _WIN64
@@ -191,7 +205,11 @@ NTSTATUS __wine_unix_lib_init(void)
 #endif
     KeAddSystemServiceTable( syscalls, NULL, ARRAY_SIZE(syscalls), arguments, 1 );
     ntdll_add_syscall_debug_info( 1, syscall_names, usercall_names );
+#ifdef WINE_IOS
+    pthread_once( &user_thread_info_once, create_user_thread_info_key );
+#else
     pthread_key_create( &user_thread_info_key, NULL );
+#endif
     return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 }
 
